UIF-OS v6

UNIVERSAL INTELLIGENCE DATA ACQUISITION, EVIDENCE, PROVENANCE & SCIENTIFIC ANALYSIS SYSTEM

Revision: 6.0.0
Architecture: Provider-Agnostic / Evidence-Controlled / Provenance-Preserving
Acquisition Domain: Public or explicitly authorized data
Analytical Model: T0 Observation → T1 Deterministic Derivation → T2 Probabilistic Analysis
Security Model: Zero Trust / Deny by Default / Least Privilege / Fail Closed
Reproducibility: Hash-Addressed / Versioned / Replayable
Epistemic Requirement: Every assertion must resolve to inspectable supporting artifacts

---

00. SCIENTIFIC PURPOSE

UIF-OS is an evidence-controlled computational system for:

1. discovering legitimately accessible information sources;
2. acquiring source observations;
3. preserving source material without destructive mutation;
4. recording acquisition context;
5. validating source and response integrity;
6. normalizing heterogeneous information;
7. generating deterministic derived features;
8. performing explicitly labeled probabilistic analysis;
9. preserving complete provenance and lineage;
10. detecting conflicts, anomalies, duplicates, and schema drift;
11. supporting reproducible analytical replay;
12. exporting evidence packages with machine-verifiable integrity;
13. maintaining a complete audit trail of system behavior.

UIF-OS MUST distinguish:

OBSERVATION
    !=
TRANSFORMATION
    !=
INFERENCE
    !=
HYPOTHESIS
    !=
DECISION

No inference may be represented as an observation.

No probabilistic output may modify the underlying observation.

No source-quality score may be treated as proof of truth.

No model-generated statement may become evidentiary merely because a model produced it.

---

01. EPISTEMIC ARCHITECTURE

01.1 Evidence classes

T0 = SOURCE OBSERVATION

T1 = DETERMINISTIC DERIVATION

T2 = PROBABILISTIC ANALYSIS

T0

T0 represents what the acquisition system actually received or directly measured.

Examples of T0-level fields include:

source_identifier
source_uri
retrieval_timestamp
HTTP_status
content_type
content_length
raw_payload
payload_hash
source_timestamp
publication_timestamp
response_metadata
connector_identifier
connector_version
request_identifier

T0 MUST be immutable after acceptance.

T1

T1 represents transformations whose output can be reproduced from:

input_artifact_hashes
+
transformation_version
+
parameters
+
execution_environment

Examples:

canonicalization
normalization
unit conversion
timestamp normalization
exact deduplication
field extraction
statistical aggregation
hash generation
schema mapping
deterministic feature calculation

T2

T2 represents analytical interpretation.

Examples:

classification
ranking
semantic similarity
hypothesis generation
probabilistic scoring
anomaly interpretation
natural-language synthesis
model-generated summaries

T2 MUST contain:

model_identifier
model_version
input_artifact_ids
input_hashes
prompt_or_instruction_hash
generation_parameters
timestamp
confidence_metadata
uncertainty_metadata
provenance references

---

02. CORE SCIENTIFIC INVARIANTS

The following invariants are mandatory.

I-001  Every accepted observation has provenance.

I-002  Every T1 artifact identifies all parent artifacts.

I-003  Every T2 artifact identifies the evidence on which it depends.

I-004  T0 artifacts cannot be silently mutated.

I-005  T0 artifacts cannot be overwritten by T1 or T2.

I-006  T2 outputs cannot be represented as direct observations.

I-007  Conflicting observations are retained rather than silently erased.

I-008  Every transformation is versioned.

I-009  Every connector is versioned.

I-010  Every schema is versioned.

I-011  Every export is integrity-verifiable.

I-012  Secrets never enter evidence, logs, telemetry, or exports.

I-013  Unauthorized acquisition is structurally denied.

I-014  Provider capabilities are discovered rather than assumed.

I-015  Provider quotas are discovered rather than hard-coded as facts.

I-016  Model availability is validated at execution time.

I-017  Network destinations are explicitly validated.

I-018  Failed validation produces rejection or quarantine.

I-019  Replay metadata is preserved.

I-020  Configuration changes are auditable.

I-021  External content cannot redefine system policy.

I-022  Data quality metadata cannot silently alter source evidence.

I-023  Provenance is preserved across every transformation boundary.

I-024  Every scientific claim is traceable to one or more artifacts.

I-025  Unsupported certainty is prohibited.

