06. GOOGLE GEMINI PROVIDER

GEMINI_ENABLED="true"

GEMINI_PROVIDER_ID="google_gemini"

GEMINI_API_BASE_URL="https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com"

GEMINI_AUTH_MODE="${GEMINI_AUTH_MODE}"
GEMINI_CREDENTIAL_REFERENCE="${GEMINI_CREDENTIAL_REFERENCE}"

GEMINI_CAPABILITY_DISCOVERY="true"
GEMINI_MODEL_DISCOVERY="true"
GEMINI_RUNTIME_MODEL_VALIDATION="true"

GEMINI_PRIMARY_MODEL="${GEMINI_PRIMARY_MODEL}"
GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL="${GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL}"

GEMINI_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT_ENABLED="true"
GEMINI_EMBEDDING_ENABLED="true"
GEMINI_REASONING_ENABLED="${GEMINI_REASONING_ENABLED}"

GEMINI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS="${GEMINI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS}"

GEMINI_MAX_RETRIES="${GEMINI_MAX_RETRIES}"
GEMINI_RETRY_BASE_MS="${GEMINI_RETRY_BASE_MS}"
GEMINI_RETRY_MAX_MS="${GEMINI_RETRY_MAX_MS}"

GEMINI_CIRCUIT_BREAKER_ENABLED="true"

GEMINI_RESPONSE_CACHE_ENABLED="true"
GEMINI_RESPONSE_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS="${GEMINI_RESPONSE_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS}"

GEMINI_COST_GUARD_ENABLED="true"

GEMINI_DAILY_COST_LIMIT_USD="${GEMINI_DAILY_COST_LIMIT_USD}"

Critical correction

Do not encode current model availability as an immutable application fact.

Instead:

CONFIGURED_MODEL
        |
        v
CAPABILITY DISCOVERY
        |
        +---- available ----> EXECUTABLE
        |
        +---- unavailable --> FALLBACK / DENY

Google's current model catalog is dynamic: it currently lists Gemini 3.8 Flash as stable, Gemini 3.1 Pro as preview, and identifies multiple older models as shut down.

Therefore:

GEMINI_PRIMARY_MODEL="${operator_selected_model}"

is scientifically preferable to embedding an asserted "current" model into application logic.

---

07. GEMINI QUOTA MODEL

The original fixed values:

MAX_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=10
MAX_REQUESTS_PER_DAY=1000
MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=1000000

MUST NOT be interpreted as provider facts.

Instead:

GEMINI_QUOTA_DISCOVERY="true"

GEMINI_RPM_LIMIT="${DISCOVERED_RPM}"
GEMINI_TPM_LIMIT="${DISCOVERED_TPM}"
GEMINI_RPD_LIMIT="${DISCOVERED_RPD}"

GEMINI_SPEND_LIMIT="${DISCOVERED_SPEND_LIMIT}"

GEMINI_QUOTA_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS="300"

GEMINI_QUOTA_FAIL_SAFE="true"

Google documents RPM, TPM, and RPD as separate rate-limit dimensions and states that limits vary according to model and usage tier; it also states that limits can change as the project's tier/account status changes.

Therefore the system MUST distinguish:

PROVIDER_DOCUMENTED_LIMIT
        !=
CURRENT_PROJECT_LIMIT
        !=
APPLICATION_LIMIT
        !=
OBSERVED_EFFECTIVE_LIMIT

All four should be independently recorded.

