18. CLAIM OBJECT

Every externally presented scientific claim SHOULD resolve to:

{
  "claim_id": "...",
  "claim_text": "...",
  "claim_type": "observed|derived|inferred|hypothesized",
  "evidence_artifacts": [],
  "source_references": [],
  "method_reference": "...",
  "transformation_reference": "...",
  "model_reference": null,
  "timestamp": "...",
  "confidence": null,
  "uncertainty": null,
  "contradicting_evidence": [],
  "status": "..."
}

The phrase:

"the data proves X"

MUST NOT be generated unless the underlying methodology explicitly establishes what "proves" means.

Prefer:

"Artifact A records X."

"Transformation T derives Y from A."

"Analysis M assigns probability/confidence Z to hypothesis H."

"Source B conflicts with source A on field F."

