19. SOURCE CONFLICT MODEL

Conflicts MUST be represented as data.

{
  "conflict_id": "...",
  "artifact_a": "...",
  "artifact_b": "...",
  "field": "...",
  "values": [],
  "observed_at": [],
  "conflict_type": "...",
  "resolution_status": "unresolved|resolved|superseded",
  "resolution_method": "...",
  "resolution_basis": [],
  "decision_artifact": "..."
}

No source may disappear solely because another source has a higher trust score.

---

20. SOURCE TRUST MODEL

Trust MUST be decomposed.

Possible dimensions:

identity_assurance
provenance_quality
publication_transparency
historical_reliability
technical_integrity
timeliness
independence
corroboration
completeness
known_limitations

A single composite score MUST NOT be presented as an objective measure of truth.

Instead:

TRUST_PROFILE
    |
    +-- identity
    +-- provenance
    +-- integrity
    +-- timeliness
    +-- corroboration
    +-- limitations

---

21. DATA QUALITY MODEL

Required dimensions:

COMPLETENESS
VALIDITY
ACCURACY
CONSISTENCY
UNIQUENESS
TIMELINESS
CONFORMITY
INTEGRITY
PROVENANCE

Each dimension MUST preserve:

metric_definition
measurement_method
sample_or_population
measurement_timestamp
result
threshold
uncertainty

A data-quality score is metadata about the dataset.

It is not a substitute for the dataset.

---

22. TEMPORAL MODEL

Every timestamp MUST identify its semantic meaning.

event_time
publication_time
source_update_time
retrieval_time
processing_time
analysis_time
export_time

These MUST NOT be conflated.

All timestamps SHOULD use RFC 3339/UTC canonical storage while preserving original source timezone information where available.

---

23. CACHE MODEL

Cache entries MUST distinguish:

CACHE_KEY
SOURCE_ID
REQUEST_FINGERPRINT
RESPONSE_HASH
CREATED_AT
EXPIRES_AT
PROVIDER_VERSION
SCHEMA_VERSION
CONNECTOR_VERSION

A cache hit MUST remain distinguishable from a live acquisition.

LIVE_RETRIEVAL
CACHE_REPLAY
REPLAY_FROM_ARCHIVE

are different acquisition states.

---

24. RETRY MODEL

Retries MUST be classified.

TRANSIENT_NETWORK_FAILURE
TIMEOUT
RATE_LIMIT
SERVER_ERROR
AUTHENTICATION_FAILURE
AUTHORIZATION_FAILURE
INVALID_REQUEST
NOT_FOUND
POLICY_DENIAL
INTEGRITY_FAILURE

Only explicitly retryable classes may be retried.

Google documents 429 rate-limit responses and recommends waiting/retrying with exponential backoff; 401, 403, 404, and model-not-found conditions have different semantics and should not be treated as generic transient failures.

---

25. CIRCUIT BREAKER

CIRCUIT_BREAKER_ENABLED="true"

FAILURE_THRESHOLD="${FAILURE_THRESHOLD}"
SUCCESS_THRESHOLD="${SUCCESS_THRESHOLD}"

OPEN_DURATION_MS="${OPEN_DURATION_MS}"

HALF_OPEN_ENABLED="true"

SCOPE="provider|connector|endpoint"

The circuit state MUST be observable and auditable.

---

26. RATE GOVERNANCE

RATE_LIMITER_ENABLED="true"

RATE_LIMIT_ALGORITHM="token_bucket"

RESPECT_PROVIDER_LIMITS="true"

RESPECT_ROBOTS_POLICY="true"

RESPECT_TERMS_POLICY="true"

JITTER_ENABLED="true"

ADAPTIVE_RATE_CONTROL_ENABLED="true"

RATE_LIMIT_STATE_PERSISTENCE="true"

Application limits and provider limits MUST be modeled independently:

effective_limit =
MIN(
    provider_limit,
    project_limit,
    connector_limit,
    operator_limit,
    safety_limit
)

The calculation itself MUST be recorded.

---

27. QUOTA GOVERNANCE

QUOTA_GUARD_ENABLED="true"

QUOTA_DISCOVERY_ENABLED="true"

QUOTA_RESERVATION_ENABLED="true"

QUOTA_ESTIMATION_ENABLED="true"

QUOTA_CONSUMPTION_RECORDING_ENABLED="true"

QUOTA_EXHAUSTION_ACTION="DENY"

AUTOMATIC_BILLING_ESCALATION="false"

No system may infer that a provider offers "free" usage solely from the absence of a configured price.

---

28. COST ACCOUNTING

Each billable operation SHOULD record:

provider
project
model
operation
input_units
output_units
cached_units
estimated_cost
actual_cost_when_available
currency
billing_timestamp
cost_source

Distinguish:

ESTIMATED_COST
ACTUAL_BILLED_COST

They are not equivalent.

---

29. DEDUPLICATION

Deduplication MUST preserve originals.

EXACT_DUPLICATE
CANONICAL_DUPLICATE
NEAR_DUPLICATE
SEMANTIC_SIMILARITY
POSSIBLE_DUPLICATE

No probabilistic match may destroy the underlying artifacts.

---

30. ANOMALY DETECTION

An anomaly MUST be represented as:

{
  "anomaly_id": "...",
  "population_definition": "...",
  "baseline": "...",
  "observed_value": "...",
  "expected_value": "...",
  "method": "...",
  "threshold": "...",
  "uncertainty": "...",
  "artifact_references": [],
  "status": "detected|investigating|resolved|false_positive"
}

An anomaly is a deviation under a specified model.

It is not automatically evidence of misconduct, causation, intent, or compromise.

---

31. REPLAY MODEL

Replay MUST capture:

SOURCE ARTIFACTS
CONFIGURATION
CONFIG HASH
CONNECTOR VERSION
SCHEMA VERSION
TRANSFORMATION VERSION
MODEL IDENTIFIER
MODEL VERSION
PROMPT HASH
PARAMETERS
DEPENDENCIES
RUNTIME VERSION
ENVIRONMENT METADATA
RANDOMNESS STATE WHEN APPLICABLE
OUTPUT HASHES

Replay results MUST be classified:

BITWISE_IDENTICAL
SEMANTICALLY_EQUIVALENT
NON_IDENTICAL
NON_REPRODUCIBLE

A newer provider model MUST NOT be silently substituted during historical replay.

---

32. AUDIT MODEL

Every security-sensitive operation MUST produce an audit event.

{
  "audit_id": "...",
  "timestamp": "...",
  "actor": "...",
  "principal_type": "...",
  "action": "...",
  "resource": "...",
  "request_id": "...",
  "correlation_id": "...",
  "result": "...",
  "reason": "...",
  "policy_version": "...",
  "config_hash": "...",
  "artifact_references": []
}

Secrets and authentication material MUST be redacted before serialization.

---

33. QUARANTINE

Quarantine MUST occur for:

INVALID_SCHEMA
INVALID_PROVENANCE
HASH_MISMATCH
POLICY_FAILURE
AUTHORIZATION_FAILURE
MALFORMED_RESPONSE
SUSPICIOUS_NETWORK_DESTINATION
UNTRUSTED_REDIRECT
DATA_CORRUPTION
INCOMPLETE_ARTIFACT
UNRESOLVED_INTEGRITY_FAILURE

Quarantine is not deletion.

The quarantined artifact MUST retain:

artifact_id
reason
timestamp
detector
rule_version
original_hash
source_reference

